# Tests of the `cprocess` module; generated from tools/cprocess.dsl by tools/build.py. They run under
# `refined test`, where machine and system targets work in the JIT's own process.

signalTest is test
signalTest purpose "signal gives back the handler it replaced, and raise of an ignored signal returns 0; system(NULL) finds a shell"
signalTest verifies setHandler installsHandlers
signalTest verifies raiseSignal raisesSignals
signalTest verifies runCommand runsShell
signalTest typeParameter none
signalTest input none
signalTest output none
signalTest outputOwnedBy none
signalTest raises none
signalTest effect use machine.memory
signalTest effect use system.calls
signalTest uses memoryAccess
signalTest uses systemCalls
signalTest memoryHeap false
signalTest async false
signalTest maxRecursion none
signalTest label begin loopKind none
signalTest label begin within none
signalTest let one Int64 1 immutable
signalTest let int3210 Int32 10 immutable
signalTest let int320 Int32 0 immutable
signalTest let int321 Int32 1 immutable
signalTest let int32Minus1 Int32 -1 immutable
signalTest at begin do readIgnore
signalTest at begin do readFirst
signalTest at begin do readSecond
signalTest at begin do doAssertTrueStep1
signalTest at begin do doAssertTrue
signalTest at begin do readRaised
signalTest at begin do doAssertTrueStep2
signalTest at begin do doAssertTrue2
signalTest at begin do readUnusedSetHandler
signalTest at begin do readNowhere
signalTest at begin do readShell
signalTest at begin do doAssertTrueStep3
signalTest at begin do doAssertTrue3
signalTest at begin do readBad
signalTest at begin do doAssertTrueStep4
signalTest at begin do doAssertTrue4
signalTest at begin return ok none

readIgnore is call
readIgnore in signalTest
readIgnore invokes machine.fromInt64
readIgnore argument value Int64 one copy
readIgnore result ignore machine.Address
readIgnore ownedBy none
readIgnore cleanedBy none
readIgnore borrows none
readIgnore catch none
readIgnore suppresses none

